  'gautrain-operating-contract-new-15-year-consortium-2026-09-30',
  'Gautrain''s operating contract awarded to new 15-year consortium',
  'Traffic', '2026-09-30', 'BusinessTech', 'https://businesstech.co.za/news/?p=877647',
  'Gauteng has appointed the Sihamba Sonke Mobility consortium to run the Gautrain for the next 15 years, with a bigger train fleet planned.',
  'Gauteng has awarded the Gautrain''s operating contract for the next 15 years to a new consortium, as the rail system''s long-running agreement with its original operator comes to an end.

The Gauteng provincial government said on 30 September that it had concluded the process to appoint the Sihamba Sonke Mobility consortium, made up of partners including Alstom, RATP Dev and GIBB-Crede, to run, maintain and upgrade the Gautrain for the period from 2026 to 2041. The new arrangement took effect on 28 September, when a holdover period under the previous operator, Bombela, ended.

Commuters in Pretoria, Centurion and Johannesburg can expect a bigger service over the life of the contract: the fleet of four-car trains will grow from 24 to 32, a jump of roughly a third, alongside more frequent off-peak trains, longer operating hours and extra feeder-bus routes. Stations are also set to get upgrades such as expanded Wi-Fi and new ticketing technology, rolled out in phases rather than all at once.

Since the Gautrain opened in 2010, it has carried more than 216 million passenger trips. An SSM investment principal, Mpho Mutloane, said the consortium''s focus was on "ensuring continuity, maintaining standards commuters expect and investing in the system."',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://businesstech.co.za/news/?p=877647", "https://www.engineeringnews.co.za/article/gauteng-secures-gautrain-operator-to-support-next-phase-of-growth-modernisation-2026-10-01"]',
  'agent'
